<title>BULGARIA: Yield down to 0.40 pct on Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield down to 0.40 pct on Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yield fell further to 0.40 percent on Bulgaria's Finance Ministry four-week discount T-bills at the daily auction on Wednesday, central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>The average yield to maturity at Tuesday's auction was 0.42 percent, down from 0.47 percent on Monday and 0.58 on Friday.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with a par value of 10 billion levs and no minimum acceptable price set in advance.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3040297007</p>
<p> Maturity			four weeks</p>
<p> Par value		     10,000 million levs</p>
<p> Issue date		    June 26</p>
<p> Maturity date		 July 24</p>
<p> Bids received		 7,500 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   99.60 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 7,500 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  99.60 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     0.40 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
